  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.0,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.07,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.97–1.0 from 6 h onward. A plateau like that could be reader saturation hiding continued growth, so I diluted the retained aliquots to test it. At 18 h, the 10x dilution read 0.106 (×10 = 1.06) and the 30x dilution read 0.032 (×30 = 0.95). At 12 h, the 10x dilution read 0.099 (×10 = 0.99). All the diluted readings, scaled back up, come to about 1.0, which matches the undiluted ~0.97. If the reader were saturating, the scaled-up diluted values would be well above the undiluted ones. The small differences between the scaled values (0.95–1.06) are within replicate noise. The plateau is therefore real stationary phase at OD ~1, and the undiluted readings are accurate."
  },
